 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nOptimizer functions broken after removing conditional checks\n\n#### Description\n\nThe SQL optimizer is throwing errors when processing queries. Several optimizer functions are failing with `NameError` and `AttributeError` exceptions.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\nfrom sqlglot import optimizer\n\n# Basic optimization fails\ntry:\n    result = optimizer.optimize('SELECT * FROM table1 t1 JOIN table2 t2 ON t1.id = t2.id')\n    print(\"Success:\", result.sql())\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Error:\", e)\n\n# Table isolation fails  \ntry:\n    from sqlglot.optimizer.isolate_table_selects import isolate_table_selects\n    query = sqlglot.parse_one(\"SELECT * FROM users u\")\n    result = isolate_table_selects(query)\n    print(\"Success:\", result.sql())\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Error:\", e)\n\n# Join optimization fails\ntry:\n    from sqlglot.optimizer.optimize_joins import optimize_joins\n    query = sqlglot.parse_one(\"SELECT * FROM a CROSS JOIN b\")\n    result = optimize_joins(query)\n    print(\"Success:\", result.sql())\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Error:\", e)\n```\n\nThe code above should work but instead throws various errors like `NameError: name 'references' is not defined` and `AttributeError` exceptions.\n</issue>\n",
